// RUN: rm -f tiling_dyn.ll
// RUN: FILE=%s;%mim -p opt -o - ${FILE%_run.mim}.mim -p ll
// RUN: clang tiling_dyn.ll -o %t -Wno-override-module
// RUN: %t ; test $? -eq 0
// RUN: %t x ; test $? -eq 0
// RUN: %t x y z ; test $? -eq 0

// Compiles tiling_dyn.mim (the full Tileable feature set over runtime-only extents) to
// an executable and runs it for the runtime sizes n = 5, 7 and 11 (n = 2·argc + 3).
// Every demo is self-checking against an untiled reference - blocked matmul (rows
// padded to a multiple of 4, i/j/k tiled, interchanged), partial reduction (reduction-
// tile loop outermost, trailing partials merged), transposed write map under a runtime
// batch, peel main/epilogue, pad+slice, a tiled pure-loop nest, and the shape-
// polymorphic tile4_for at a runtime size - so the expected exit code is simply 0.
